  "result": "I've fixed both seat-counting problems. The code type-checks, but I haven't run the test suite.\n\n1. **Removing a member now frees their seat right away.** In `src/server/services/usage-service.ts`, removing a member now takes one seat off the workspace's usage immediately (there was already a matching step that adds a seat when someone joins). The periodic recount in `src/server/repositories/usage-repository.ts` used to count every membership row, including removed ones. It now counts only active members who haven't been removed.\n2. **Revoked invitations no longer hold a seat.** The pending-invitation count in `src/server/repositories/invitation-repository.ts` now leaves out revoked invitations as well as accepted ones. This also fixes re-sending an invitation in a full workspace, since the old one is revoked when the new one is created. A workspace that really is full is still refused, because active members plus pending invitations are still checked against the plan limit.",
